{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/SQ","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/SH","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/SY","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/13SwiftProtobuf4EnumP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For elements it selects between reviving the element already in the tree and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserting a copy of it. The copy is what undo does today, and because a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deep copy keeps every descendant’s created_at, it puts a second live element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under ids the document is indexed by. Reviving needs a replicated liveness"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"register – removed_at paired with revived_at on each element – so that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every replica resolves a remove\/revive race the same way, with a tie going","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the removal as the shipped remove register already does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The branch cannot be chosen from local state. A replica that collected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between the removal and the undo has purged the tombstone, and one that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joined from a later snapshot never had it, so “revive if a tombstone is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present” is a function of local collection timing and the same change log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would produce different documents. That is why the branch is on the wire."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode","symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode"}],"externalID":"s:6Yorkie0A15_V1_RestoreModeO"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_restoremode"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RestoreMode selects the identity-preserving path. RESTORE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means an ordinary edit (no restore semantics), keeping forward edits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unchanged on the wire."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/UNRECOGNIZED(_:)","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/restore","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/retombstone","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/unspecified"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/init()","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/rawValue-